[{"id":81182,"sender_id":11,"sender_full_name":"Urs","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b00d1ee17463af676c78974439b92471?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/15-Mathematics.2C-Physics-.26-Philosophy/topic/Pro-finite.20su.282.29-representations.3F/near/81182\">#1</a> In order to formalize some physics, I am looking for a suitable mathematical concept. It looks like the putative concept ought to be something like “pro-finite <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"fraktur\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"fraktur\">u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathfrak{su}(2)</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathfrak\">su</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">2</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>-representations”, but I am not sure yet. And once I am sure, I’ll be wondering if there is any decent established theory for such things.</p>\n<p>The following is the motivation (taken from <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model#M2M5BraneBoundStatesInTheBMNMatrixModel\">here</a>):</p>\n<p><strong>Motivation</strong></p>\n<p>There is the remarkable observation (<a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model#MSJVR02\">MSJVR 02</a>, checked in <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/BMN+matrix+model#AIST17\">AIST 17</a>) that in the <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/BMN%20matrix%20model\">BMN matrix model</a> supersymmetric <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/M2-M5-brane%20bound%20states\">M2-M5-brane bound states</a> are identified with “limit sequences” of <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/isomorphism%20classes\">isomorphism classes</a> of <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/finite-dimensional%20vector%20space\">finite-dimensional</a> <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/complex%20numbers\">complex</a> <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Lie%20algebra%20representations\">Lie algebra representations</a> of <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/su%282%29\">su(2)</a>.</p>\n<p>Concretely, if</p>\n<p><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">{</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo separator=\"true\">,</mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">}</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">≔</mi></mo><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mo lspace=\"0.22em\" rspace=\"0.22em\"><munder><mo><mo>⊕</mo></mo><mi>i</mi></munder></mo><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>⋅</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><msubsup><mi>N</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>M</mi><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></msub><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mo>∈</mo><mtext>  </mtext><mtext>  </mtext><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"fraktur\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"fraktur\">u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\n  \\mathbf{N}( \\{N^{(M2)}_i,N^{(M5)}_i\\}_i )\n  \\;\\;\\coloneqq\\;\\;\n  \\underset{ i }{\\oplus}  N^{(M2)}_i \\cdot \\rho_{N^{(M5)}_i}\n  \\;\\;\\in\\;\\;\n  \\mathfrak{su}(2)\\mathrm{Rep}^{\\mathrm{fin}}\n</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.3217em;vertical-align:-0.2769em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">N</span><span class=\"mopen\">({</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.0448em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4231em;margin-left:-0.109em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.2198em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mopen mtight\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">2</span><span class=\"mclose mtight\">)</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2769em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">N</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.0448em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4231em;margin-left:-0.109em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><spa